{# Generic UCRem Fix Template - used for all document types #}
{% extends "ucrem/base.md.j2" %}

{% block fix_guidelines %}
## {{ doc_type | upper }} Fix Guidelines

### Auto-Safe Fixes (HIGH Confidence)
- Formatting corrections (whitespace, indentation)
- ID pattern fixes ({{ doc_type | upper }}.XX.YY format)
- Missing required fields with obvious values
- Broken reference repairs
- Typo corrections

### Manual Review Fixes (MEDIUM Confidence)
- Content additions to incomplete sections
- Restructuring of requirement statements
- Acceptance criteria improvements
- Traceability additions

### Expert Review Fixes (LOW Confidence)
- Semantic requirement changes
- Priority reassignments
- Scope modifications
- Architectural changes

### {{ doc_type | upper }}-Specific Rules
1. Preserve existing {{ doc_type | upper }}.XX.YY IDs when possible
2. Maintain traceability chain integrity
3. Keep requirement atomicity
4. Ensure testability preserved
{% endblock %}

{% block instructions %}
## {{ doc_type | upper }} Remediation Instructions

### Phase 1: Critical Fixes (P0)
1. Address all P0 findings first
2. Each fix must resolve one finding
3. Validate no regression introduced

### Phase 2: Major Fixes (P1)
1. Address P1 findings by impact
2. Consider cumulative changes
3. Check for fix conflicts

### Phase 3: Minor Fixes (P2)
1. Apply formatting fixes
2. Correct documentation issues
3. Polish and consistency

### Quality Checks
- [ ] All P0 findings addressed
- [ ] Traceability preserved
- [ ] ID patterns valid
- [ ] No orphaned requirements
- [ ] Schema compliance maintained

### Iteration {{ iteration }}/{{ max_iterations }}
{% if iteration > 1 %}
Previous iteration made progress. Focus on remaining findings.
{% endif %}
{% if iteration == max_iterations %}
**Final iteration**: Prioritize P0 fixes only. Document any unresolved P1/P2 for manual review.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
